<div class="how-it-works">
  <h2 class="how-it-works__title">How It Works</h2>
  <p class="how-it-works__subtitle">Three steps. No learning curve. No fear.</p>

  <div class="how-it-works__steps">
    <div class="how-it-works__step">
      <div class="how-it-works__number">1</div>
      <h3 class="how-it-works__step-title">Drop Your Vegetable In the Top</h3>
      <p class="how-it-works__step-desc">The food hopper holds it securely in place. Cucumbers, potatoes, carrots, sweet potatoes — anything you'd normally slice by hand.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="how-it-works__step">
      <div class="how-it-works__number">2</div>
      <h3 class="how-it-works__step-title">Press Down With Both Hands</h3>
      <p class="how-it-works__step-desc">Your hands grip the top handle and push straight down. They stay 8+ inches above the blade the entire time. No guard needed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="how-it-works__step">
      <div class="how-it-works__number">3</div>
      <h3 class="how-it-works__step-title">Perfect Slices Collect Below</h3>
      <p class="how-it-works__step-desc">Uniform, restaurant-thin slices land in the catch tray. Adjust the dial for paper-thin to thick gratin cuts. Done in under 3 minutes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="how-it-works__footer">That's it. Your hands never go near the blade. Not during slicing. Not during cleanup.</p>
